  "configuration_id": "config_043",
  "reason": "Evidence: The largest single-factor improvement observed so far is the RNA encoder swap from pca_n2000 to scvi_n200 in the multimodal/multiprofile/avgpool/weighted setup (config_019→config_031: +3.9% acc, +2.7% F1). We have zero data on the scgpt encoder. Question: Does scgpt outperform scvi_n200 as the RNA encoder in the currently best configuration? Why this experiment: config_043 is an isolated, controlled comparison against config_031—only the RNA encoder changes. This resolves the highest-uncertainty, highest-impact design choice (RNA encoder) in the context where it matters most. If scgpt wins, we have a new best and a direction to exploit; if it loses, we confirm scvi_n200 is optimal and can redirect remaining budget toward the image encoder (resnet50 vs imagenet_vit_l) or aggregation strategy. Under a limited budget, this single experiment maximally reduces uncertainty about the most influential factor."
}

